raised for the subtlety of its psychological approach, mixes autobiographical elements and obvious references to Latin literature. It is preserved here in a manuscript copied in 1467 by Giovanni Cardello da Imola, whose regular calligraphy is set off by decorations in bianchi girari (white vine-stem).</dc:description><dc:format>95 ff., 26.5 x 17.2 cm</dc:format><dc:identifier>doi:10.5076/e-codices-fmb-cb-0039</dc:identifier><dc:identifier>http://www.e-codices.unifr.ch/en/list/one/fmb/cb-0039</dc:identifier><dc:identifier>Cologny, Fondation Martin Bodmer, Cod. Bodmer 39</dc:identifier><dc:publisher>e-codices - Virtual Manuscript Library of Switzerland</dc:publisher><dc:language>Italian</dc:language><dc:relation>Allegretti Paola, Catalogo dei codici italiani, Cod. Bodmer 39, in "Corona Nova. Bulletin de la Bibliotheca Bodmeriana", II (2003), pp. 39-40.</dc:relation><dc:rights>e-codices / Cologny, Fondation Martin Bodmer (cf. http://www.e-codices.unifr.ch/en/about/terms)</dc:rights><dc:source rdf:resource="http://www.e-codices.unifr.ch/en/list/one/fmb/cb-0039"></dc:source><dc:title>Cologny, Fondation Martin Bodmer, Cod. Bodmer 39 : Giovanni Boccaccio, Elegia di madonna Fiammetta</dc:title><dc:type>Manuscript</dc:type><dcterms:medium>Parchment</dcterms:medium><edm:europeanaProxy>false</edm:europeanaProxy><ore:proxyFor rdf:resource="http://data.europeana.eu/item/9200211/en_list_one_fmb_cb_0039"/><ore:proxyIn rdf:resource="http://data.europeana.eu/aggregation/provider/9200211/en_list_one_fmb_cb_0039"/><edm:type>TEXT</edm:type></ore:Proxy><ore:Proxy rdf:about="http://data.europeana.eu/proxy/europeana/9200211/en_list_one_fmb_cb_0039"><dc:coverage rdf:resource="http://data.europeana.eu/place/92"></dc:coverage><dc:date rdf:resource="#1467"></dc:date><dc:type rdf:resource="http://data.europeana.eu/concept/17"></dc:type><dcterms:medium rdf:resource="http://data.europeana.eu/concept/2092"></dcterms:medium><edm:europeanaProxy>true</edm:europeanaProxy><edm:year>1467</edm:year><ore